In the diagram, what is the perimeter of polygon $PQRST$?

[asy]
import olympiad;

size(6cm); // ADJUST

pair p = (0, 6);
pair q = (5, 6);

pair r = (5, 1);
pair t = (0, 0);
pair s = (8, 0);

draw(p--q--r--s--t--cycle);
label("$P$", p, NW);
label("$Q$", q, NE);
label("$R$", r, E + NE);
label("$S$", s, SE);
label("$T$", t, SW);

label("$6$", p / 2, W);
label("$5$", p + (q - p) / 2, 2 * N);
label("$8$", s / 2, S);

draw(rightanglemark(p, t, s));
draw(rightanglemark(t, p, q));
draw(rightanglemark(p, q, r));
add(pathticks(p--q, s=6));
add(pathticks(q--r, s=6));
[/asy]

The hexagon with the label G is colored green. Each hexagon is colored either green, blue, or orange, such that no two hexagons with a common side are colored the same color. In how many different ways can the figure be colored?

[asy]
path a=(0,0)--(10,0)--(15,8.7)--(10,17.3)--(0,17.3)--(-5,8.7)--cycle;
draw(a);
draw(shift((15,8.7))*a);
draw(shift((15,-8.7))*a);
draw(shift((30,17.3))*a);
draw(shift((30,0))*a);
draw(shift((30,-17.3))*a);
draw(shift((45,26))*a);
draw(shift((45,8.7))*a);
draw(shift((45,-8.7))*a);
draw(shift((60,17.3))*a);
draw(shift((60,0))*a);
draw(shift((60,-17.3))*a);
draw(shift((75,8.7))*a);
draw(shift((75,-8.7))*a);
label("$G$",(5,10),S);
[/asy]

What is the area, in square units, of triangle $ABC$?
[asy]
unitsize(1.5mm);
defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(8pt));
dotfactor=4;

pair A=(-2,3), B=(6,3), C=(3,-4);
pair[] dots={A,B,C};
real[] xticks={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7};
real[] yticks={4,3,2,1,-1,-2,-3,-4,-5};

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
dot(dots);

label("A(-2,3)",A,N);
label("B(6,3)",B,N);
label("C(3,-4)",C,S);

xaxis(-4,8,Ticks(" ", xticks, 3),Arrows(4));
yaxis(-5,5,Ticks(" ", yticks, 3),Arrows(4));
[/asy]

Find the length of $XY$ in the triangle given below.

