Assume a square ABCD. Points P and Q are located one third along AB from A, and two thirds along BC from B, respectively. What fraction of the interior of the square is shaded if the region inside the square but outside the triangle APQ is shaded?

[asy]
filldraw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--(0,0)--cycle,gray,linewidth(1));
filldraw((0,1)--(2,3)--(3,3)--(0,1)--cycle,white,linewidth(1));
label("P",(0,1),W);
label("Q",(2,3),N);
[/asy]

In the diagram, triangles $PQR$ and $STU$ are shown with given side lengths in centimeters. What is the length of segment $PQ$?

[asy]
pair P,Q,R,S,T,U;

P=(0,0);
Q=8*dir(0);
R=12*dir(60);
S=6+Q;
T=S+4*dir(0);
U=S+6*dir(60);

draw(P--Q--R--cycle);
draw(S--T--U--cycle);

label("P",U,N);
label("Q",T+(1.4,0));
label("4",.5*(P+Q),S);
label("10",.5*(Q+R),NE);
label("8",.5*(P+R),NW);
