In the diagram below, $\overline{AB}\parallel \overline{CD}$ and $\angle AXF = 135^\circ$. Another line $\overline{EZ}$ intersects $\overline{CD}$ at point $Z$. Given that $\angle FZD = 45^\circ$, find $\angle FYD$.

[asy]
unitsize(1inch);
pair A,B,C,D,X,Y,EE,F,Z;
A = (0,0);
B=(1,0);
C = (0,0.8);
D=(1,0.8);
EE = (0.35,-0.3);
F = (0.8,1.1);
Z = (0.65,0.8);  // New point Z
draw(EE--F);
draw(A--B);
draw(C--D);
draw(F--Z, dashed);  // New line FZ
dot(A);
dot(B);
dot(C);
dot(D);
dot(EE);
dot(F);
dot(Z);  // Place dot at Z
label("$E$",EE,S);
label("$F$",F,N);
X = intersectionpoint(A--B,EE--F);
Y = intersectionpoint(C--D,EE--F);
label("$X$",X,NNW);
label("$Y$",Y,NNW);
label("$A$",A,W);
label("$B$",B,E);
label("$C$",C,W);
label("$D$",D,E);
label("$Z$",Z,N);  // Label Z
dot(X);
dot(Y);
[/asy]

In the diagram, $D$ and $E$ are the midpoints of $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{BC}$ respectively. Determine the sum of the $x$ and $y$ coordinates of $F$, the point of intersection of $\overline{AE}$ and $\overline{CD}$. Given:
- Point $A$ is at $(0,8)$
- Point $B$ is at $(0,0)$
- Point $C$ is at $(10,0)$ [asy]
size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(10pt));
pair A, B, C, D, E, F;
A=(0,8);
B=(0,0);
C=(10,0);
D=(0,4);
E=(5,0);
F=(10/3,16/3);
draw(E--A--C--D);
draw(D--B, dashed);
draw((-1,0)--(12,0), EndArrow);
draw((0,-1)--(0,9), EndArrow);
label("$A(0,8)$", A, NW);
label("$B(0,0)$", B, SW);
label("$C(10,0)$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, W);
label("$E$", E, S);
label("$F$", F, NE);
label("$x$", (12,0), dir(0));
label("$y$", (0,9), dir(90));
[/asy]

