Lines $l$ and $m$ are parallel. A line $n$ intersects these lines forming angles where $m\angle A = 140^\circ$ on line $l$. Line $m$ is further intersected by a line $p$ at point $C$ on $m$, creating angle $m\angle C = 70^\circ$. Determine $m\angle B$ if line $p$ also intersects line $l$ at point $D$ such that lines $n$ and $p$ are not parallel.

[asy]
size(100); real h = 1.2; currentpen = fontsize(10pt);
draw(Label("$l$",Relative(1)),(0,0)--(1,0),E);
draw(Label("$m$",Relative(1)),(0,-h)--(1,-h),E);
draw(Label("$n$",Relative(0.5)),(0,0)--h/2*(cos(130*pi/180),sin(130*pi/180)) + (0,-h),W);
draw(Label("$p$",Relative(0.3)),(0,-h)--h*sqrt(3)/2*(cos(-110*pi/180),sin(-110*pi/180)),E);
label("$A$",(0,0),N); label("$B$",(0,-h),S);
label("$140^\circ$",(h/4, -h/4),NE); label("$70^\circ$",h*sqrt(3)/4*(cos(-110*pi/180),sin(-110*pi/180))+(0.1,-0.3),W);
[/asy]

Circles $A$, $B$, and $C$ are externally tangent to each other. Circle $A$ has a radius of 2. Circle $B$ has a radius of 1, and is externally tangent to an additional circle $E$, which also touches circle $A$ externally. All circles are in the same plane. Find the radius of circle $C$.

[asy]
unitsize(1cm);
pair A,B,C,E;
A=(0,0);
B=(3,0);
C=(1.5, 1.3228756555);
E=(-1,0);
draw(Circle(A,2),linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(B,1),linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(C,0.5),linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(E,1),linewidth(0.7));
label("$A$",A,W);
label("$B$",B,E);
label("$C$",C,N);
label("$E$",E,W);
[/asy]

