The length of the shortest trip from $A$ to $C$ along the edges of a cube shown is the length of 4 edges. How many different 4-edge trips are there from $A$ to $C$?

[asy]
size(4cm,4cm);
pair a1, b1, c1, d1;
a1=(1,1);
b1=(0,1);
c1=(1.6,1.4);
d1=(1,0);
pair e1, f1, g1, h1;
e1=(0,0);
f1=c1-(a1-d1);
g1=b1+(c1-a1);
h1=e1+(g1-b1);
draw(a1--d1--e1--b1--a1);
draw(b1--g1--c1--a1);
draw(c1--f1--d1);
draw(g1--h1--e1,dotted+1pt);
draw(h1--f1,dotted+1pt);
label("$A$",e1,SW);
label("$C$",f1,NE);
[/asy]

