for(int i=0; i < 4; ++i){
for(int k=0; k < 6; ++k){
draw((0,i)--(5,i));
draw((k,0)--(k,4));
} }

draw((0,0)--(2,4));
draw((4,4)--(5,0));

label("$P$",(0,0),SW);
label("$Q$",(5,0),SE);
label("$R$",(5,4),NE);
label("$S$",(0,4),NW);
label("$T$",(2,4),N);

[/asy]
```

A square and an isosceles right triangle are inscribed in a circle. The square and triangle share a common vertex. If the hypotenuse of the isosceles right triangle coincides with one side of the square, what is the number of degrees in the angle directly opposite the shared vertex inside the triangle?

[asy]
import markers; defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
pair A,B,C,D,E,F;
draw(unitcircle);

A=(-1,0);
B=(0,-1);
C=(1,0);
D=(0,1);

draw(A--B--C--D--A);

E=(-1,1);
F=(1,1);

draw(D--E--F--D);

markangle(Label("?"),n=1,radius=10,E,D,F,marker(stickframe(n=0),true));

label("$V$",D,N);
label("$X$",E,W);
label("$Y$",F,E);
[/asy]

$ABCD$ is a rectangle whose area is 20 square units. How many square units are contained in the area of trapezoid $EFBA$ where $E$ and $F$ are points on $AD$ and $BC$ respectively, such that $AE = 1$ unit and $BF = 1$ unit?

[asy]
size(4cm,4cm);
for(int i=0; i < 5; ++i){
for(int k=0; k < 6; ++k){
draw((0,i)--(5,i));
draw((k,0)--(k,4));
} }
draw((0,0)--(1,4));
draw((4,4)--(5,0));
label("$A$",(0,0),SW);
label("$B$",(5,0),SE);
label("$C$",(5,4),NE);
label("$D$",(0,4),NW);
label("$E$",(1,4),N);
label("$F$",(4,4),N);
[/asy]

